P2b. Separating optimisation level from debug-assertions, because -O moves BOTH.
NOTE: an earlier version of this script looped over quoted flag strings in fish,
which does not word-split, so rustc got one bogus argument and NOTHING compiled.
The CONTROL caught it: the wide arm reported NO in all four cells, which is
impossible if the table is about the two arms. Written out explicitly below.

--- narrow arm (expected: refused wherever const-eval checks) ---
opt0 dbg-assert=off : E0080 count -, artifact 0
opt0 dbg-assert=off : artifact YES
opt0 dbg-assert=on  : artifact NO (E0080 lines 2)
opt3 dbg-assert=off : artifact YES (E0080 lines 0)
opt3 dbg-assert=on  : artifact NO (E0080 lines 2)
o1 runs -> if this printed, the const channel does not distinguish: 900000000
o3 runs -> if this printed, the const channel does not distinguish: 900000000

--- CONTROL: the wide arm must compile under all four ---
wide arm artifacts: opt0/off YES  opt0/on YES  opt3/off YES  opt3/on YES
